engine: give the host pool 94 percent instead of 75 when every layer is resident -- the 25 percent margin exists to leave room for not-yet-loaded streamed layer weights, which cannot happen when the plan already keeps all 40 layers on the card. On the L20 that margin cost 77GB, leaving the expert cache at 231GB against the 268.9GB the model needs, so warm-up could never finish and decode read from disk every step